          "skill": "Command of Evidence - Weaken",
          "domain": "Information and Ideas",
          "focus": "Identify evidence that weakens or undermines an argument or finding",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 5 · Q9",
          "passageTitle": "Command of Evidence - Weaken — Q9",
          "passage": "Students in a biology class investigated why\nindividual house mice (Mus musculus) can differ\nfrom one another in their susceptibility to\ncataracts in old age. The students compared\nwild-type mice and knockout mice, which are\nmice with specific genes deactivated, when mice\nof each type were raised in similar naturalistic\nenvironments and periodically tested for\ncataracts. Finding that knockout mice with the\ngene Aasdh deactivated tended to develop\ncataracts more frequently than did wild-type\nmice, the students concluded that differences in\ncataract frequency among house mice in nature\nare solely attributable to variations in the level\nof expression of Aasdh.",
