          "passageTitle": "Command of Evidence - Weaken — Q13",
          "passage": "Veronica L. Bura, Akito Y. Kawahara, and\nJayne E. Yack investigated the evolution and\nfunction of sound production in silk moth and\nhawk moth caterpillars. They found that during\nharmless simulated attacks on caterpillars, 33%\nof the tested species produced sound, which\nranged from clicks in Antheraea pernyi to\nwhistles in Phyllosphingia dissimilis. A second\nresearch team has claimed that caterpillars use\nthese sounds primarily to communicate with\nother members of their species.",
